            <ul style="color:#333; padding-left: 2.2%;">
                <li> Hon’ble Minister of Mines, Coal & Parliamentary affairs, Chief Minister of Madhya Pradesh along with Secretary (Mines) visited the HCL stall at ‘Mining & Beyond’ exhibition of 2nd Mining Ministers conference at Bhopal on 23.01.2024 where a miniature model of Ram Mandir, Ayodhya was displayed. Hon’ble Minister of Mines, have praised to HCL & twitted that “HCL had delivered 70,000 pure Copper Strips & 775 Copper Wire Rods, both 99.99% pure electro-refined copper, for joining the rocks in Ram Mandir construction. The highest quality copper ensures longevity, promising thousands of years for the rock joints.</li>
                <li> The Company has achieved a Profit Before Tax and Revenue from Operations of Rs 144.96 Crore and Rs. 752.34 Crore in H1 of FY 2023-24. The Profit Before Tax and Revenue from Operations are 31.28% & 34.22% higher than the corresponding period of FY 2022-23.</li>
                <li> HCL has paid dividend of Rs. 88.97 crore to its Shareholders in Oct’23 for the period of FY 2022-23.</li>
                <li> The target of Capex for FY 2023-24 is Rs. 350 Crore where HCL had achieved Rs. 416.61 Crore till January’24.</li>
